      "side": 1,
      "message": "The counters we\u0027ll end up incrementing are u64 - that\u0027s why \u0027packets\u0027 and \u0027bytes\u0027 are u64.\nSo the conversion to u64 will need to happen before the next line finishes anyway.\nAnd then it gets added into bytes on the line after that, which would require u64+u32 calculation which will just get boosed to u64 again.\n\nSo basically I don\u0027t think there\u0027d be any actual benefit to making this narrower, and indeed it might be worse.  Remember that bpf is a 64-bit VM/bytecode.",
